
========================================================================
  THE DROWNED TOWER
  Fort on the Lake: the island and the first cellars
========================================================================
Seed: 1

== The Fort Docks ==
(The Fort, noon)

The Fort docks. Captain Maren coils a wet rope and does not smile.

MAREN: Row to the Isle of Old Stone. Find out who lands there, and what
moves in the water.

One boat. One hero. Maren waits to hear who goes.

Who rows to the Isle of Old Stone? [final]
  1. The Fighter
     A sword and 8 hit points. Strong at doors.
  2. The Wizard
     A dagger, 4 hit points, and one Sleep spell.
> 2

You tuck the dagger in your belt. The word of Sleep waits behind your
teeth.

== The Broken Jetty ==
(The Isle of Old Stone, sunset)

Four hours of oars later, the sun is low and the island is close.

A stone jetty runs out from the south shore. Half of it has fallen into
the lake.

On a mooring post, a rope burn shows pale and fresh: someone else lands
here.

Past the end of the jetty, something large moves under the water, a long
shadow, and is gone.

Role: wizard

Where do you go? [plan]
  1. Walk up to the tower shell
  2. Row back to the Fort
     The delve ends here.
> 1

== The Tower Shell ==
(The Isle of Old Stone)

A round tower, thirty feet across, open to the sky. Its upper floors
fell in long ago and lie as rubble on the ground.

A stair climbs the inside wall to a broken top forty feet up. Crows
watch you from the rim with the calm of tax collectors.

Role: wizard

What do you look at? Looking is free. [plan]
  1. Search the rubble
  2. Climb the stair
  3. Move on
> 1

You shift stones for ten minutes. Under the rubble lies a trapdoor of
black oak.

Its iron ring is furred with rust. It lifts with a groan.

Role: wizard

Where do you go? [plan]
  1. Walk to the keeper's cottage
  2. Go down through the trapdoor
  3. Walk back to the jetty
> 1

== The Keeper's Cottage ==
(Beside the tower)

A stone cottage beside the tower. The roof is gone.

The hearth holds ash less than a week old.

A tin of lamp oil sits on a shelf, enough for two flasks.

On the door someone has chalked an eye with a line through it. It is not
a greeting.

Role: wizard

What do you do here? Looking is free. [plan]
  1. Take the tin of lamp oil
  2. Look at the chalked eye
  3. Leave it all
> 1

You take the tin. It is heavy, and the oil in it is clean.

Role: wizard

Where do you go? [plan]
  1. Go back to the tower
> 1

== The Tower Shell ==
(The Isle of Old Stone)

A round tower, thirty feet across, open to the sky. Its upper floors
fell in long ago and lie as rubble on the ground.

A stair climbs the inside wall to a broken top forty feet up. Crows
watch you from the rim with the calm of tax collectors.

The trapdoor lies open in the rubble. A stair goes down into the dark.

Role: wizard

What do you look at? Looking is free. [plan]
  1. Climb the stair
  2. Move on
> 1

From the broken top you see the whole island: rock, pine, the jetty, the
cottage.

At the north cliff a boat-shaped shadow lies on the water.

Role: wizard

Where do you go? [plan]
  1. Walk to the keeper's cottage
  2. Go down through the trapdoor
  3. Walk back to the jetty
> 2

== The Cellar Stair ==
(Under the tower)

Under the trapdoor a stone stair goes down twenty feet. The air smells
of old oil and wet stone.

At the bottom stands an oak door, swollen in its frame. It is stuck.

Role: wizard

Listen at the door first? [plan]
  1. Listen at the door
  2. Do not listen
> 1

Scratching. Squeaks. Many small feet.

Role: wizard

The door is stuck. What do you do? [final]
  1. Oil the hinges, then push
  2. Force the door
> 1

You work oil from the tin into each hinge. Then you push. The door
swings open without a sound.

== The Oil Store ==
(The first cellar)

Racks of broken oil jars. The floor is tacky.

Five giant rats, each the size of a cat, lift their heads from the
spill.

The oiled door made no sound.

Role: wizard

One rat leaps. What do you do? [final]
  1. Speak the word of Sleep
  2. Fight with your dagger
  3. Back up the stair
> 2

You strike at the first rat. It dodges. Two more come over the jars.

You fall among the broken jars. The rats close in.

************************************************************************
  AMONG THE BROKEN JARS
************************************************************************

Your torch rolls away across the oily floor and goes out.

Far above, the crows wait on the tower rim. Captain Maren will send
someone else to the island.

THE END
Trail: docks > jetty > tower > cottage > tower > cellar > store > fell
r = play again, q = quit > q
Goodbye.
